  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Deaf Education, Empowerment and Employment (Deaf-E&#xb3;)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  ..To address the needs of deaf, hard of hearing, and deafblind (D/HH/DB) children and youth in Nigeria, the Deaf-E&amp;sup3; activity will build the capacity of multiple community and professional groups: educational professionals, D/HH/DB community members and leaders, sign language interpreters, development professionals, and parents of D/HH/DB children. This will be accomplished by: (a) Providing educational professionals with training in a multimodal/multilingual pedagogical approach and co-developing two manuals on this approach, to be shared with additional professionals; (b) Developing the Nigerian National Association of the Deaf (NNAD) organizational capacity and the individual capacity of its stakeholders, and the involvement of D/HH/DB role models in educational settings with professionals, families, and their D/HH/DB children; (c) Establishing a working group of Nigerian Sign Language interpreters and deaf consumers that will analyze current and best practices related to interpreting as a whole and specific to education; and, (d) Increasing the capacity of USAID and its partners to engage D/HH/DB stakeholders nationwide, as well as enlisting support from these development actors in promoting awareness of NNAD as a resource to parents, government ministries, and others in the field of education, amplifying this activity&apos;s impact on the lives of D/HH/DB people in Nigeria....</narrative>
  </description>
